WEBVTT

1
00:00.000 --> 00:04.500
[Audio description: Three white medicine boxes sit side by side on a kitchen counter: Amlodipine 5 mg, Ibuprofen 400 mg, and Metformin 500 mg.]

2
00:04.500 --> 00:10.500
[Narrator] Three white boxes. For ~55,000 visually impaired Finns, ~45,000 aged 65+, 97% struggle to read medicine labels.

3
00:10.500 --> 00:15.000
[Narrator] And 1 in 5 Finns aged 75+, 21.6%, juggle 10 or more medicines. HoldUp: hold it up, know it's the right one.

4
00:15.000 --> 00:21.500
[Audio description: Phone shows three plain-language consent cards, HoldUp Bridge streaming HTTP 204, and Using glasses camera with the temple LED lit.]

5
00:21.500 --> 00:30.000
[Narrator] Your profile stays in on-device localStorage only. The camera runs only during a check, stops after 45 seconds, and keeps an 8-frame memory ring.

6
00:30.000 --> 00:35.000
[Narrator] Momin holds Amlodipine 5 mg backwards with both hands free and asks: "Is this my evening pill?"

7
00:35.000 --> 00:41.000
[Glasses] The label is on the other side. Turn it around... A bit closer.

8
00:41.000 --> 00:48.000
[Audio description: Green MATCH card appears on the phone and a green RIGHT ONE card lights up the 600x600 Ray-Ban Display HUD.]
[Glasses] Yes, Amlodipine 5 mg, your evening pill. You haven't taken it today.

9
00:48.000 --> 00:54.000
[Audio description: Momin pinches the Neural Band to activate "I took it", logging today's dose on the phone.]
[Narrator] One Neural Band pinch on "I took it" logs today's dose.

10
00:54.000 --> 01:00.000
[Audio description: Holding up Amlodipine a second time triggers an amber WARNING card on the phone and CHECK on the HUD.]
[Glasses] Warning: Amlodipine already taken today.

11
01:00.000 --> 01:07.500
[Audio description: Momin holds up Ibuprofen 400 mg; amber WARNING and CHECK card appears.]
[Glasses] This is Ibuprofen 400 mg. It isn't on your medication list and your list says to avoid NSAIDs.

12
01:07.500 --> 01:15.000
[Audio description: Thumb and tape cover the strength digits on Metformin; blue NOT SURE card appears with zero dose guessing.]
[Glasses] It looks like Metformin, but I can't read the strength confidently. Turn the box so the side panel faces you, or ask a pharmacist.

13
01:15.000 --> 01:20.000
[Narrator] Deterministic safety.ts enforces a < 0.8 strength gate, a < 0.95 allergen gate, and EU FMD GS1 DataMatrix (01) GTIN and (17) expiry checks.

14
01:20.000 --> 01:26.500
[Audio description: Glasses doffed while online; worn: false auto-switches the source to Phone camera.]
[Narrator] Take the glasses off while online and HoldUp auto-switches to Phone camera.

15
01:26.500 --> 01:34.000
[Audio description: Airplane mode turns ON with Bluetooth ON; scanning the Amlodipine barcode triggers an offline amber WARNING card.]
[Glasses] You're offline. Warning: Amlodipine already taken today.

16
01:34.000 --> 01:40.000
[Audio description: Airplane mode turns OFF; status recovers to Live assistant connected in under 10 seconds.]
[Narrator] Restore the network and Gemini Live reconnects in under 10 seconds.

17
01:40.000 --> 01:50.500
[Narrator] Speculative verify cuts first audio to 2.1 s median, 3.4 s p95 across 26 live sessions. Across 1,740 images: 0 of 754 confident-wrong strengths and 0.06% silent unsafe reassurance.

18
01:50.500 --> 02:00.000
[Narrator] With a 12.8 MB Verda H100 FieldSpotter ONNX model at 96.8% precision, we propose a 4-week, 20-member supervised study with Näkövammaisten liitto and Finnish pharmacies. HoldUp.
